    "title": "Pershing Square USA Ltd Files Amendment to Registration Statement - Washington Today",
    "text": "Got story updates? Submit your updates here. ›An amended SEC filing provides a rare glimpse into the intricate workings of a prominent closed-end investment fund.Washington TodayPershing Square USA Ltd, a closed-end investment company, has filed an amendment to its registration statement with the United States Securities and Exchange Commission. The updated Form N-2/A filing was submitted on April 13, 2026 under Securities Act File No. 333-294164 and 1940 Act File No. 811-23932. Why it matters As a closed-end investment fund, Pershing Square USA Ltd's registration statement and any amendments provide important transparency into the company's structure, investment strategies, and regulatory compliance. These filings are closely watched by investors, analysts, and regulators to assess the fund's activities and risk profile. The details The amended registration statement likely includes updates to Pershing Square USA Ltd's investment objectives, policies, leverage, and other key details required by the SEC for closed-end funds. Closed-end funds must regularly file these types of updates as their business evolves. Pershing Square USA Ltd filed the amended Form N-2/A on April 13, 2026. The players Pershing Square USA LtdA closed-end investment company that is required to regularly file registration statements and updates with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. Got photos? Submit your photos here. › The takeaway This amended filing provides a window into the operations and regulatory compliance of a major closed-end investment fund, offering transparency that is closely watched by industry stakeholders.",
